<div class="text guide-styles" data-units-dynamic="article" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">
<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Paladin Tank in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 4</h2>Phase 4 retains the itemization potential for <a class="icontiny c2" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=2/paladin">
<img alt="Paladin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_paladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Paladin</span></a> tanks to keep running two separate tiers in parallel in order to pick up their respective 2-set bonuses. While we don't think this is an outstanding upgrade over running Protection 4-set (which does have its uses), it is noteworthy in that the Retribution tier pieces are as ever relatively competitive.<br/>
<br/>Unless mentioned, since gear is completely shared between all difficulty modes (ilevel just scaled up between normal &amp; heroic), you can assume that the item priority is maintained through normal modes even if they are not explicitly listed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="protection-armor-of-radiant-glory">Protection <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-495/armor-of-radiant-glory">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Armor of Radiant Glory</span></a></h4>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table border="0" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="3" class="markup-table-clean-borders" style="width: 100%; max-width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 20%; max-width: 100%;">
<div class="box last" data-level="null">
<i>2 Piece Bonus</i></div></td>
<td style="width: 80%; max-width: 100%;">Your Judgement ability now also grants a physical absorbtion shield equal to 25% of the damage it dealt.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table border="0" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="3" class="markup-table-clean-borders" style="width: 100%; max-width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 20%; max-width: 100%;">
<div class="box last" data-level="null">
<i>4 Piece Bonus</i></div></td>
<td style="width: 80%; max-width: 100%;">Reduces the cooldown of Divine Guardian by 60 sec and increases the radius of its effect by 70 yards.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>2-set here adds a very nice passive survivability boon to our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85064/judgement">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_righteousfury.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Judgement</span></a>, while it's not nearly enough to turn one of our core rotative abilities into something akin to active mitigation, it is a very welcome buff that shores up some of our weaknesses.<br/>
<br/>4-piece on the other hand is more difficult to place however prior to this <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=70940/divine-guardian">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_powerwordbarrier.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Guardian</span></a> could be difficult to cast and maximize as often boss arenas are very large and your group may be scattered far beyond your reach. This helps you greatly in making sure this will consistently be up on time and reach all other players and in a lot of ways steroids the use-cases for your raid CD.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="retribution-battleplate-of-radiant-glory">Retribution <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-493/battleplate-of-radiant-glory">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Battleplate of Radiant Glory</span></a></h4>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table border="0" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="3" class="markup-table-clean-borders" style="width: 100%; max-width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 20%; max-width: 100%;">
<div class="box last" data-level="null">
<i>2 Piece Bonus</i></div></td>
<td style="width: 80%; max-width: 100%;">Your Judgement ability now also generates 1 Holy Power.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table border="0" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="3" class="markup-table-clean-borders" style="width: 100%; max-width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 20%; max-width: 100%;">
<div class="box last" data-level="null">
<i>4 Piece Bonus</i></div></td>
<td style="width: 80%; max-width: 100%;">While Zealotry is active your abilities deal 18% more damage.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>Like the Protection 2-piece, the retribution bonus inserts a valuable benefit to one of our core rotative skills and loads another huge bonus onto <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85064/judgement">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_righteousfury.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Judgement</span></a>. One of our more critical weaknesses is the RNG factor in our rotation, being heavily reliant on procs that while are relatively consistent can still leave you open for several seconds as you wait for your abilities to come off cooldown. This simply alleviates that issue (does not fix it) and should improve your playing experience.<div class="pad"></div>
